[[15,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Using a screwdriver, lift up the springs (1a) and extract the radio console (1b).</p><p>2. Open the band (2a) and release the aerial connector (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/244004699.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Secure the aerial connector using the band.</p><p>- Fit the radio console in the housing.</p>"]]